# Hexana CLI @VERSION@

This directory contains the native Hexana command-line products for the supported release platforms.

Choose the standard CLI for `summarize-binary`, `summarize-module`, and `wasm-to-wat`. Choose the script CLI for
`run-script`. Both products also provide `tools`, `version`, and `help`.

## Downloads

| Product | macOS Apple silicon | Linux x86-64 |
|---|---|---|
| `hexana-cli` | [hexana-cli-native-macos-arm64-@VERSION@.zip](@DOWNLOADS_PREFIX@/hexana-cli-native-macos-arm64-@VERSION@.zip) | [hexana-cli-native-linux-x64-@VERSION@.zip](@DOWNLOADS_PREFIX@/hexana-cli-native-linux-x64-@VERSION@.zip) |
| `hexana-cli-script` | [hexana-cli-script-native-macos-arm64-@VERSION@.zip](@DOWNLOADS_PREFIX@/hexana-cli-script-native-macos-arm64-@VERSION@.zip) | [hexana-cli-script-native-linux-x64-@VERSION@.zip](@DOWNLOADS_PREFIX@/hexana-cli-script-native-linux-x64-@VERSION@.zip) |

Every ZIP has a sibling `.sha256` file. Download both files and verify the checksum before extracting the archive:

```bash
shasum -a 256 -c hexana-cli-native-macos-arm64-@VERSION@.zip.sha256
unzip hexana-cli-native-macos-arm64-@VERSION@.zip
./bin/hexana-cli version
```

On Linux, use `sha256sum -c` instead. The extracted executable is under `bin/`. The archive also includes
`LICENSE.txt`, the product README, and `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md`.

Machine-readable release metadata is available in
[`hexana-cli-release-@VERSION@.json`](@DOWNLOADS_PREFIX@/hexana-cli-release-@VERSION@.json). When the release was also
published on GitHub, each artifact's `githubReleaseAssetUrl` field contains the corresponding alternative URL.
